{
    "background_story": "Santino was a free-spirited artist who lived life on his own terms. However, after his grandmother passed away, he felt obligatorily bound to take care of her beloved family bakery. Despite his initial reluctance, Santino discovered a new passion for traditional Italian pastries and dedicated himself to mastering the recipes. As he worked tirelessly to keep the bakery afloat, he found a sense of purpose and connection to his heritage. The bakery became a staple in the community, with customers drawn to Santino's warm hospitality and delicious creations. Though he had initially felt obligated to take on the responsibility, Santino came to realize that it was an opportunity to honor his grandmother's memory and build a new legacy of his own.",
